-- title:
--   Uniform small-parameter mean bounds imply convergence along real roots
-- statement:
--   Let $F:\mathbb R\to\mathbb R$ satisfy $F(b)\leq1$ for every $b$. Assume that for each $\varepsilon>0$, some $\delta>0$ satisfies $F(b)\geq1-\varepsilon$ whenever $|b|<\delta$. Then, for every $a\in\mathbb R$,
--   $$F(a/(n+1))\longrightarrow1.$$
--   No continuity or measurability of $F$ is required. This packages the uniform small-translation estimate for the root argument.
-- source:
--   Ruijun Wang, Comparisons of benchmark equivalence relations, Theorem 1.5 (formerly MeasureEquivalence.tex, Theorem 1.3); supporting declaration MeasureEquivalenceRigidity.tendsto_mean_along_real_roots in ComponentRigidityRoots.lean, lines 75–94; local source SHA-256 24ec0c9b1da33e69de220995790006d9c2544459a304dbb277860fefd7f782ce. Designated upload repository: https://github.com/RayjunWang/Benchmark (no source commit published yet).

